   "title": "Guide",
   "description": "The Tickory guide: for users (tasks, dates, reminders, projects, sharing, offline, the Android app) and for administrators (installing, HTTPS, backup, updating).",
   "html": "<h1>Guide</h1>\n<p class=\"intro\">Everything about using and running Tickory. Search for a word at the top left, or pick a topic below.</p>\n\n<p>This guide belongs to version 0.12.0 of Tickory. The app is bilingual: English and Dutch (choose the language in <span class=\"ui\">Settings</span>, or let it follow your browser's language). Buttons and menus are named here as they appear in the English interface. What you type (<code>tomorrow at 9am</code>, <code>every monday</code>) is recognised in the language of the app. Want to see how it works first? <a href=\"https://wnijhof.github.io/tickory/demo/?lang=en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Try the demo</a>: the real app with sample data, without a server and without an account.</p>\n<p>This guide is also in the app itself, even offline: choose <span class=\"ui\">Settings</span> and then <span class=\"ui\">Guide</span>. In the desktop app, <em>Help › Guide</em> opens it.</p>\n\n<h2 id=\"for-users\">For users</h2>\n<ul class=\"cards\">\n  <li><a href=\"#help=signing-in\"><strong>Signing in</strong><span>What you need, and what to do when it does not work.</span></a></li>\n  <li><a href=\"#help=adding-tasks\"><strong>Adding tasks</strong><span>Type one line with project, section, label, priority, date and reminder.</span></a></li>\n  <li><a href=\"#help=dates-and-recurrence\"><strong>Dates and recurrences</strong><span>Every form the app understands, with examples.</span></a></li>\n  <li><a href=\"#help=the-screen\"><strong>The screen: sidebar and task list</strong><span>Inbox, Today and Upcoming, favorites, the circles and chips, ticking off.</span></a></li>\n  <li><a href=\"#help=projects\"><strong>Projects and sections</strong><span>Colors, subprojects, favorites, archiving, the project menu and sections.</span></a></li>\n  <li><a href=\"#help=views\"><strong>List, board and calendar</strong><span>A project as a board with columns or as a calendar by month or week; dragging cards and tasks, also with the keyboard.</span></a></li>\n  <li><a href=\"#help=labels\"><strong>Labels</strong><span>Keywords on tasks: all tasks with a label, and making, renaming, coloring and deleting labels.</span></a></li>\n  <li><a href=\"#help=search\"><strong>Search</strong><span>Search tasks, comments, projects and labels with / or Ctrl+K, with the words found highlighted.</span></a></li>\n  <li><a href=\"#help=filters\"><strong>Filters</strong><span>Saved searches in a filter language of their own, with checking while you type and examples.</span></a></li>\n  <li><a href=\"#help=task-window\"><strong>The task window</strong><span>Editing a task: date, priority, labels, subtasks and comments.</span></a></li>\n  <li><a href=\"#help=attachments\"><strong>Attachments</strong><span>Photos and files on a task, also choosable offline; viewing, saving and deleting.</span></a></li>\n  <li><a href=\"#help=reminders\"><strong>Reminders</strong><span>A notification at the moment you need to do something, in your browser or in the Android app.</span></a></li>\n  <li><a href=\"#help=shortcuts\"><strong>Keyboard shortcuts</strong><span>q, g then t, u or i, / or Ctrl+K, ? and Ctrl+Enter: faster with the keyboard.</span></a></li>\n  <li><a href=\"#help=sharing\"><strong>Sharing and working together</strong><span>Sharing a project, assigning tasks, and what stays personal.</span></a></li>\n  <li><a href=\"#help=offline\"><strong>Working offline</strong><span>What happens without a connection and when everything syncs.</span></a></li>\n  <li><a href=\"#help=install-as-app\"><strong>Install as an app</strong><span>On your phone and on your computer.</span></a></li>\n  <li><a href=\"#help=android-app\"><strong>Android app</strong><span>An app of its own with reminders as alarms on your phone, widgets and more. The APK is on the releases page.</span></a></li>\n  <li><a href=\"#help=browser-extension\"><strong>Browser extension</strong><span>Save the page you are reading, a link or selected text as a task with one click, in Chrome, Edge and Firefox.</span></a></li>\n  <li><a href=\"#help=account\"><strong>Account, password and devices</strong><span>Changing your password, signing devices out and choosing the language.</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2 id=\"for-administrators\">For administrators</h2>\n<ul class=\"cards\">\n  <li><a href=\"#help=installing\"><strong>Installing with Docker</strong><span>Setting up the server and creating the first account.</span></a></li>\n  <li><a href=\"#help=managing-users\"><strong>Managing users</strong><span>Creating and blocking accounts, and resetting passwords.</span></a></li>\n  <li><a href=\"#help=sign-in-with-sso\"><strong>Signing in with SSO</strong><span>Signing in with your own sign-in service (OpenID Connect).</span></a></li>\n  <li><a href=\"#help=https\"><strong>HTTPS</strong><span>Needed for phones and for notifications in the browser: with Tailscale, a reverse proxy or a tunnel.</span></a></li>\n  <li><a href=\"#help=updating\"><strong>Updating</strong><span>Installing a new version, and upgrading from version 0.1.</span></a></li>\n  <li><a href=\"#help=backup\"><strong>Backup and restore</strong><span>Making a safe copy and putting it back.</span></a></li>\n  <li><a href=\"#help=troubleshooting\"><strong>Troubleshooting</strong><span>Common messages and what to do about them.</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>What Tickory cannot do yet is listed on the <a href=\"https://wnijhof.github.io/tickory/en/index.html#not\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">home page</a>. That is meant honestly: better to know up front than to find out later.</p>",
